*Week 10 - Software Testing*

Given the following code, choose the correct statement about mocking:

```java
@Mock private BookRepository books;
@InjectMocks private BookServiceImpl bookService;

@Test
void addBook_ShouldSaveAndReturnBook...() {
    Book book = new Book("This is a New Title");
    when(books.findByTitle(any(String.class)))
        .thenReturn(Collections.emptyList());
    when(books.save(any(Book.class)))
        .thenReturn(book);

    Book savedBook = bookService.addBook(book);

    assertNotNull(savedBook); // more assertions needed...
    // verify
    verify(books).findByTitle(book.getTitle());
    verify(books).save(book);
}
```

*Week 11 - Code Review, Refactoring and Pair Programming*

How to refactor the following code:

```java
int discount(int inputVal, int quantity, int yearToDate) {
    if (inputVal > 50) inputVal -= 2;
    if (quantity > 100) inputVal -= 1;
    if (yearToDate > 10000) inputVal -= 4;
    return inputVal;
}
```
